# `$hasContiguousIndex(array, i)` asks whether the list holds integers or values one behind the other. Of the kinds of a list these two alone lack one bit,
# whatever the bits of the byte outside the kind say. So the byte is not cut down to the kind first: a load and a test of the bit.
# RUN: emit f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK: @[[byte]] = Load8Z({{*}}JSArray_indexingTypeAndMisc
# CHECK-NEXT: = BitAnd(@[[byte]],
# PROGRAM-OF: element-that-a-test-has-found-in-a-plain-vector-is-not-loaded-again.ir
